<title>SPAIN: EU seen agreeing stability pact in Dublin - Caruan.</title>
<headline>EU seen agreeing stability pact in Dublin - Caruan.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain expects an agreement to be reached on a stability pact at next week's Dublin summit, said Jaime Caruana, general director of the Spanish Treasury.</p>
<p>He said many steps had already been taken and that at the end, European countries would reach an agreement on fiscal delinquency.</p>
<p>&quot;Germany wants clears rules, which is an interesting idea...At the same time we, should take into account the history of economics (too),&quot; Caruana told Reuters in an interview recorded for Reuters Financial Television.</p>
<p>-- Tiziana Barghini, Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
